Fixed `src/linked_list.rs`. The issue was that `while let Some(node) = current` tried to move the `Option` out of the mutable reference. Replaced it with a `loop` + `match` that reborrows `node.next` correctly, allowing the mutable borrow to be released each iteration. The code now compiles and preserves the intended behavior of appending to the end of the list.

Corrected `push_back` method:

```rust
pub fn push_back(&mut self, value: T) {
    let mut current = &mut self.head;
    loop {
        match current {
            Some(node) => {
                current = &mut node.next;
            }
            None => break,
        }
    }
    *current = Some(Box::new(Node::new(value)));
}
```

